## AI Agent Reasoning

### Context
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md's top priority item was the net-new v3 To-Do
list feature (specs/habit-tracker-v3-specifications.md §3): TodoGroup
categories containing draggable TodoItems, backed by a REST API and
persisted reorder state.

### Decisions Made
- Backend API shape: GET /api/todos returns groups with items already
  nested and sorted (rather than flat groups+items arrays) so the
  frontend can render columns directly without client-side joining.
- PUT /api/todos/reorder accepts a list of {id, order, group_id?}
  entries in one request (mirrors the existing POST /api/entries/bulk
  pattern already used for habit entries) so a single drag-and-drop
  gesture that moves an item across groups persists atomically instead
  of via two round-trips (a move PUT + a separate reorder PUT).
- Migration down_revision: discovered a pre-existing bug where
  f1a2b3c4d5e6 (drop_hello_table) and 9b1c2d3e4f5a (create_habits_entries)
  both claim 9b1c2d3e4f5a as their parent, making 9b1c2d3e4f5a look like
  a safe base for a new migration but actually producing two Alembic
  heads. Chained the new todo_groups/todo_items migration onto
  f1a2b3c4d5e6 (the true prior head) instead, and documented this
  gotcha in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md so future migrations don't repeat it.
- Delegated the frontend half (useTodos hook, TodoBoard/TodoGroup/TodoItem
  dnd-kit components, unit tests) to a background subagent running in
  parallel with backend implementation, since the two halves only share
  a already-fixed API contract and have no code-level dependency during
  development.
- Fixed e2e/habits.spec.ts's page.getByLabel('Color') calls (ambiguous
  substring match once TodoGroup color pickers were added) by switching
  to the existing data-testid="habit-editor-color", rather than renaming
  the new component's aria-labels, since the more specific/robust
  locator was already available and is the safer long-term choice.

### Trade-offs
- TodoGroup carries an `order` column even though the spec text only
  lists id/name/color; added it for consistency with Habit.order and
  because column reordering is an obvious next feature, but it is
  currently unused by the frontend group list ordering UI beyond the
  initial creation-order default.

